ce  first had tech companies need to make  sure that they can serve ads as fast as  possible when a user opens a page  delivering ads faster translates to a  better user experience making potential  customers more likely to click on ads  and improve roi for advertisers  in practice this means that many ad tech  companies need database requests to have  latency on the order of single digit  milliseconds  bigtable is a great option for this use  case since it's designed to support  large numbers of reads and writes per  second at low latency  tech companies also need a database that  can scale  they might have billions of ad requests  per day and millions of requests per  second  this kind of extremely high throughput  might overwhelm many on-premise or  traditional databases luckily bigtable  is designed for this exact use case it  supports up to millions of read and  write requests per second and can store  up to petabytes of data  throughput can be adjusted dynamically  by adding or removing bigtable nodes  each of which provides up to 10 000  digital queries per second as well as  additional storage capacity ad tech  companies also want to focus on their  core technology like the machine  learning algorithms used to optimize ad  placement rather than worry about how to  manage their underlying database  infrastructure  as a fully managed database service  bigtable makes it easy for development  teams to focus on innovation rather than  reinventing the wheel  bigtable replicates data across multiple  google data centers all around the world  to maintain high availability and low  latency for users everywhere  this makes it easy for ad tech companies  to seamlessly expand to new markets  without having to worry about managing  the data centers themselves  bigtable also handles backups so ad tech  companies can easily recover from  application level data corruption as  well as human error  ad tech companies also find bigtable  useful because of how easy it is to  integrate with other google cloud  products  some companies have used memory store  from memcached to cache frequently query  data  this can help get latency down to lower  than one millisecond and also help  optimize bigtable costs  other companies have also extensively  used bigquery google cloud's large-scale  data warehouse for storage and analysis  while bigtable can handle very high  throughput at low latency  bigquery can be better for large scale  data analysis  in the ad tech space bigquery can be  helpful for data scientists who may want  to compile analytics and dashboards to  help advertisers and publishers meet  their goals  powerful and complex queries that may  take several minutes to complete with  other databases may take just seconds  with bigquery  and finally  tech companies rely heavily on machine  learning to take the data that's  available and use it to better connect  advertisers and potential customers  vertex ai is google cloud's unified  machine learning platform that makes it  easy for businesses to build deploy and  scale ml models on google's  infrastructure  as you can see bigtable's speed  scalability and reliability make it a  great fit for the unique challenges of  ad tech  if you're curious to learn more take a  look at the links below  thanks for joining us today and take a  look at the other episodes in the series  to learn more about bigtable
 

